<Base
  title="About findbyface — AI Face Search for OnlyFans"
  description="Learn what findbyface is, how our AI face-matching works, and the principles behind our private, free lookalike finder."
  canonical="https://findbyface.org/about/"
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>About <span class="gradient-text">findbyface</span></h1>
      <p>The fastest way to find OnlyFans creators who look just like the face in any photo.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What is findbyface?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>findbyface</strong> is a search engine for OnlyFans creators, built two ways. You can
        <a href="/onlyfans-search/">search or browse by name and category</a>, ranked by real
        engagement, or upload a photo on our <a href="/onlyfans-finder-by-face/">AI face search</a> to
        instantly find creators who share similar facial features — same eyes, smile, and overall
        look. It's built for discovery: whether you spotted someone on social media, have a celebrity
        crush, or simply want to find creators that match your type, we help you find them in seconds.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also run a separate <a href="/pornstar-finder-by-face/">pornstar finder</a>, currently in
        private beta. Upload a photo or video screenshot and it searches faces against a growing index
        of adult videos, returning matches grouped by video and ranked by visual similarity — useful
        for finding a scene when you only have a screenshot, not a name.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Browsing and search results are ordered by <strong>FindRank</strong>, our engagement-based
        ranking — no human editor decides the order. Face search runs on a separate AI pipeline: when
        you upload a photo, a face-recognition model detects the face and converts it into a numeric
        descriptor — a mathematical fingerprint of facial geometry — then compares that descriptor
        against creator profiles to rank the closest visual matches. No names, reverse lookups, or
        personal data are required. For the full breakdown of both systems, see
        <a href="/how-our-search-engine-works/">how our search engine works</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Sponsored placements</h2>
      <p>
        findbyface is free to use, partly because creators can pay for a specific, disclosed
        placement — like the top of a category page. Sponsorship never changes a FindRank or
        face-match score and never hides organic results; every sponsored card is labeled
        "Sponsored" or "Ad". Full details are on the
        <a href="/how-our-search-engine-works/">methodology page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy first</h2>
      <p>
        Your uploaded photo is processed to generate matches and is not stored or shared. There's no
        account required to run a search, and we don't sell your data. Read more in our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Important note on results</h2>
      <p>
        findbyface returns creators who <strong>visually resemble</strong> an uploaded face. Matches
        are based on appearance and are intended for discovery and entertainment only — they are
        <strong>not</strong> a confirmation of identity. A high match percentage does not mean two
        people are the same person.
      </p>

      <h2>Who's behind this</h2>
      <p>
        findbyface is built and maintained by <a href="/blog/author/nick/">Nick</a>, including
        FindRank and the disclosed sponsor model described above.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, feedback, or a content concern? Visit our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>,
        or review our <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> and
        <a href="/dmca/">DMCA policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
